desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Absolute URLs"
	title_zh: "检测到Absolute URLs",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-absolute-urls"
	risk: "best-practice"
	desc: <<<DESC
### 规则说明
Using absolute URLs to Salesforce Pages is bug prone. Different sandboxes and production environments will have different instance names (like "na10", "na15" etc.). Code using absolute URLs will only work when it runs in the corresponding salesforce instances. It will break as soon as it is deployed in another one. Thus only relative URLs, i.e. without the domain and subdomain names, should be used when pointing to a salesforce page.

### 风险类型
最佳实践（best-practice）

### 影响
代码或配置不符合推荐实践，长期来看可能引入安全或维护风险。

### 检测方式
Source 模式正则匹配，检测代码或配置中符合该风险模式的位置。

### 补充说明
Note: original paths.exclude ['*Test*', '*test*'] not applied (SF path filter limitation).

### 参考
- CWE: -
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
### 修复建议
按官方推荐方式改写，并补充必要的安全配置。
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.cls": <<<POS
http://nZXvisualforce.com.................

POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*.cls}.pattern_regex(/(http|https):\/\/.*(salesforce|force|visualforce)\.com\.*/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Absolute URLs",
	title_zh: "检测到Absolute URLs",
	message: "Absolute URLs",
}
